      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-322288",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{\u2032}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{\u2032}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{7/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{3t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"
